 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 268,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Platelets ≥ 450 × 10⁹/L (extreme ≥ 1000): is it REAL, REACTIVE or CLONAL?",
   "lines": [
    "1 · REPEAT the CBC: is it persistent? · spurious (rare): red cell fragments, cryoglobulins, bacteria counted as platelets",
    "history + exam look for reactive AND clonal causes together",
    "ALL three LOW (pancytopenia)? ↓ production (marrow) · ↑ destruction (immune, drugs, infection) · big spleen"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_r",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 702,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "2 · REACTIVE: far more COMMON · look first",
   "lines": [
    "also: hyposplenism (splenectomy, sickle cell) · non-blood cancer · rebound after myelosuppression",
    "treat the cause, then REPEAT the CBC: still high → CLONAL"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_c",
   "x": 787,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 464,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "3 · CLONAL: myeloproliferative neoplasm (MPN)",
   "lines": [
    "which other line is up? Hb ↑↑ → ERYTHROCYTOSIS chart · WBC ↑↑, Philadelphia + → CML (LEUKEMIA chart)"
   ]
  },
  {
